\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. From trials unexempted
\par Thy dearest children are;
\par But let us not be tempted
\par Above what we can bear;
\par Exposed to no temptation
\par That may our souls  o'erpower,
\par Be Thou our strong salvation
\par Through every fiery hour.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Ah! leave us not to venture
\par Within the verge of sin;
\par Or if the snare we enter,
\par Thy timely help bring in;
\par And if Thy wisdom try us,
\par Till pain and woe are past,
\par Almighty Love, stand by us,
\par And save from first to last.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Fain would we cease from sinning
\par In thought, and word, and deed;
\par From sin in its beginning
\par We languish to be freed;
\par From every base desire,
\par Our fallen nature's shame,
\par Jesus, we dare require
\par Deliverance in Thy name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. For every sinful action
\par Thou hast atonement made,
\par The perfect satisfaction
\par Thy precious blood has paid:
\par But take entire possession;
\par To make an end of sin,
\par To finish the transgression,
\par Most holy God, come in!
\par                            Amen. \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

